# ── 2026-09-15: the alternative was tried on HW and REVERTED ──────────────
# Setting CONFIG_NSH_BUILTIN_AS_COMMAND=n + CONFIG_LIBC_EXECFUNCS=y does fix
# the "cmd &" abort described below (openvela 7d54946ab compiles out the
# builtin-spawn dispatch that terminates nsh_execute()'s background-wrapper
# recursion), and the board boots and networks with it -- BUT every attempt to
# actually dispatch a builtin then wedges the whole system:
#
#   sh  -c "free"      -> g_system_ticks frozen (system dead, no ping)
#   sh  -c "free &"    -> same
#   lvgldemo (task_spawn of a plain non-NSH builtin, 32 KB registered stack)
#                      -> same, wedged at ~5.3 s right at the spawn
#
# i.e. on this port nsh_fileapp()->task_spawn() of a builtin hangs, which would
# take down ai_agent / lvgldemo / camera (the demo's whole app set).  That is
# strictly worse than the "&" abort, so keep the in-process dispatch.
#
# The "&" abort is fully root-caused in docs/05 §23.10; re-validating the
# nsh_fileapp route needs a working console (see §23.11) before it is retried.
CONFIG_NSH_BUILTIN_AS_COMMAND=y
